<title>ALGERIA: Broken Hill well hits oil in Algeria.</title>
<headline>Broken Hill well hits oil in Algeria.</headline>
<dateline>ALGIERS 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state firm Sonatrach and the Australian oil and mining company Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd (BHP) have struck oil at a test well, producing an initial 5,570 barrels a day at a wellhead pressure of 90 bars, Algeria's energy ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In a statement carried by the official news agency APS, the ministry said the discovery, the third this year, was made at an exploration well in Bir Sif Fatima Nord in the Erg Oriental (Eastern Erg) region, near the border with Libya.</p>
